+Let $(M,g,N)$ be the Schwarzschild exterior datum with $s>0$ and $f(r)=1-s/r$ on $r>s$. Let $\gamma(\lambda)$ be an affinely parametrized null geodesic of its metric-selected connection whose image lies in the equatorial plane $\vartheta=\pi/2$, choose the affine-parameter orientation so that $E>0$, and independently choose the sense of the azimuthal coordinate (replacing $\varphi$ by $-\varphi$ if needed) so that
 
 $$E:=f(r)\frac{dx^0}{d\lambda}>0,\qquad L:=r^2\frac{d\varphi}{d\lambda}\ge0.$$
 
