 1.1 In each equatorial spherical chart the components in [F1] are independent of $x^0$ and $\varphi$, and the coordinate components of $\partial_0$ and the axial generator $\partial_\varphi$ are constant. The flow pullback derivative in [F2] therefore gives $\mathcal L_{\partial_0}g=\mathcal L_{\partial_\varphi}g=0$, so both fields are locally Killing. By the conservation part of [F2] and the affine geodesic equation [F3], $-g(\partial_0,\gamma')=f\,dx^0/d\lambda=E$ and $g(\partial_\varphi,\gamma')=r^2d\varphi/d\lambda=L$ are constant on each chart interval; longitude charts differ by additive constants, so these values agree on overlaps and are constant along $\gamma$. [given, F1, F2, F3, algebra]
 
+1.2 The nonzero null tangent has nonzero time component: if $dx^0/d\lambda=0$, the positive spatial block of the exterior metric and the null condition would force every tangent component to vanish. Hence the conserved $E$ of step 1.1 is nonzero, and reversing the affine parameter if necessary makes it positive. This reversal also changes the sign of $L$; independently replace the azimuthal coordinate by $-\varphi$ if that resulting constant $L$ is negative. This angular reflection leaves the displayed metric, equatorial plane and radial equation invariant and sends $L$ to $-L$ while leaving $E$ fixed. Thus the two stated sign choices are available for every such ray; when $L=0$ no angular reflection is needed. [given, F1, step 1.1, algebra]
